# The lamp housings, which emit as well as reflect — the emissive is why the fittings read as
# the source of the light rather than as objects lit by it.
#
# ⚠ The emissive is a luminance in cd/m², not a multiplier, because everything else in this level is
# photometric: the sun is fourteen thousand lux and the tonemap is exposed at EV 11.6, so an
# emissive of 6 would come out black. Forty thousand nits is a sodium floodlight's lens seen
# directly — two orders past what the exposure can hold, which is the point: it clips, and the
# !Bloom node's threshold of three thousand is what turns that clipped core into a glow rather than
# a white square. The colour is the 1900 K arc the light beside it declares.
shader: ForwardPlus
shading: StandardShading
features:
  - !MetalRoughness
    baseColor: 0.16 0.15 0.14
    metalness: 0.6
    roughness: 0.40
  - !Emissive
    emissiveColor: 1.0 0.52 0.20
    intensity: 40000
